# prompts_things.py: Part 23's Codex prompt per things sheet (<work>/things/sheets/<s>/prompt.txt)
import json, os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
from kitlib import work
os.chdir(work('things'))
HEAD = """Use your built-in image_gen tool (not a CLI or script fallback) to make ONE image, then copy the generated image file to ./out.png in the current working directory. Do not write any code to draw it.

Three images are attached.
- guide.png: a {W} x {H} sheet on flat pure green (#00FF00) with {n}: simple 3D block-model renders of {what}, objects from a video game, seen from the game's isometric camera (from the south-east and above; height is not foreshortened). The renders are only a rotoscope guide.
- classic.png: the same {objs} as the old 8-bit game drew them, flat from the front. This is their identity: keep their look, details and colours.
- style.png: figures from the same game, already redrawn in the target style. Match THEIR pixel art style, pixel size, outlines and shading exactly.

Redraw {every} of guide.png IN PLACE, at exactly the same position, size and angle as in the guide, as hand-placed PIXEL ART in the style of style.png. The pixel grid matters most: one art pixel is exactly 10 x 10 pixels of the sheet{sizes}: count them; one art pixel is never smaller or larger than 10 x 10. 16-bit console era quality, crisp square pixels on that one even grid, like a skilled pixel artist drew it by hand. Use the render only for the shape, the angle and the volume. It must NOT look like a 3D render: no smooth gradients, no glossy highlights, no soft blur, no plastic look. Use clusters of flat colour with hand-placed shading and texture (wood grain, cloth weave, scuffs), light from the upper left, a dark outline (#0b0616 near-black violet) around each object, in each part's darkest shade where it meets another part, as in style.png.

{desc}

No text other than what is asked, no labels, no frames, no ground shadow, no ground under the objects. The background must stay flat pure green #00FF00 everywhere around the objects, and no pure green #00FF00 inside them. Many colours are welcome.
"""
